{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"despotic-dorsal-greatdane","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe real-artifact oracle from closed ticket ducal-statuelike-ladybird is valuable, but tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py independently archives the repository and runs python -m build several times. A current macOS job spent 24.34s, 15.53s, and 14.83s in three visible cases, over 54 runner-seconds before the remaining cases. No existing ticket owns test-fixture reuse.\n\n## Plan\nShare immutable clean-source/archive and eligible base-build artifacts at module/session scope, while retaining independent real builds for distinct observable contracts: wheel-from-sdist provenance, empty-env failure, sdist contents, and rebuild-from-sdist preservation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every existing real wheel/sdist assertion remains and still executes the relevant build boundary.\n- [ ] Clean source extraction and identical prerequisite builds are not repeated per test.\n- [ ] A defect-seeded missing COMMIT still fails the held-out oracle.\n- [ ] Packaging tests remain hermetic and do not reuse artifacts across pytest sessions.","id":"1c79-1d10-26b0-4a4e","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["ci","performance","tests","packaging"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Reuse build-provenance fixtures while preserving real wheel and sdist coverage"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786598923483139001,"uuid":"9ceee607-4be4-49cc-8edb-da00488c77b6"}